<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.10.3: Comparing Functions Represented in Separate Graphs</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01027</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.10.3: Comparing Functions Represented in Separate Graphs</md:title>
    <md:uuid>92e8dfd0-6db9-43e8-9a0b-7395bb5f18ae</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">The number of people who watched a TV episode is a function of that show’s episode number. Here are three graphs of three functions—<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>—representing three different TV shows.</para>
        <para id="para-00002">Show A <media alt="10 data points on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_06_01.svg"/></media></para>
        <para id="para-00003">Show B <media alt="A graph. "><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_06_02.svg"/></media></para>
        <para id="para-00004">Show C <media alt="10 data points on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_06_03.svg"/></media></para>
      
      <para id="para-00005">Match each description with a graph that could represent the situation described. One of the descriptions has no corresponding graph.</para>
      <section id="sect-00002">
     
        <exercise id="_55e82363-cfbc-47ef-9686-e02aaf346a67" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00006">This show has a good core audience. It had a guest star in the fifth episode that brought in some new viewers, but most of them stopped watching after that.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00007">Correct! The graph of function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00008">Nice try! The correct answer is: graph of function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_3d080c5a-8054-479a-9f61-4bd9fa4b3120" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00009">This show is one of the most popular shows, and its audience keeps increasing.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00010">Correct! no match</para>
            <para id="para-00011">Nice try! The correct answer is: no match</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="bfa3a562-185d-4ba8-b510-49dbc5bb5223" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00012">This show has a small audience, but it’s improving, so more people are noticing.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00013">Correct! The graph of function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00014">Nice try! The correct answer is: graph of function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_3c5faec7-0e76-4ed2-a378-ea37bb6269a1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00015">This show started out huge. Even though it feels like it crashed, it still has more viewers than another show.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00016">Correct! The graph of function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00017">Nice try! The correct answer is: graph of function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_074f8390-8547-4d20-a6b1-175f0c152fbf" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00018">Which is greatest, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00019">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00020">Nice try! The correct answer is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00001">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00021">Explain what the answer to question 5 tells us about the shows.</para>
            
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00022">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00023">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.
    3.6 million people watched the 7th episode of Show B.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Use the Desmos graphing tool or technology outside the course to sketch a graph of the viewership of the fourth TV show that did not have a matching graph. 
 </item>
      </list>
      <media alt=""><iframe src="../../media/desmos/a59acb00a5280744c0480cc59ede55347c17f6f3.html" width="500" height="400"/></media><!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      
        <exercise id="exer-00002">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00024">When you have finished graphing, select the Solution button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00025">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00026">
                      <media alt="Discrete function. episode number and audience in millions.">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_06_04.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Interaction End --><section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Video: Comparing Functions Represented in Separate Graphs</title>
      <para id="para-00027">Watch the following video to learn more about how to compare functions that are represented in separate graphs.</para>
      <media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text">
        <iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7529123fb47025e11d6485c60baf00b6394e707b"/>
      </media>
    </section>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
          <para id="para-00028">For which of the following functions is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> the greatest value?</para>
        </note>
        <section id="sect-00004">
          <title>Additional Resources</title>
          
    <section id="sect-00005">
      <title> Comparing Real-Life Functions</title>
      <para id="para-00029">Two people, Adam and Bianca, are competing to see who can save more money in one month. Use the table and the graph below to determine who will save more money at the end of the month. State how much money each person had at the start of the competition. (Assume each is following a linear function in his or her saving habit.) Let Adam’s function be represented by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, where <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is days, and Bianca’s function be represented by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00030">
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_08_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00031">
          <media alt="TWO FUNCTIONS REPRESENTING SAVINGS IN DOLLARS AS A FUNCTION OF NUMBER OF DAYS FOR TWO PEOPLE: ADAM AND BIANCA. THE TOTAL AMOUNT ADAM HAS SAVED IS REPRESENTED BY THE GRAPH OF A LINE THAT PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (0, 3) AND (2, 9). THE TOTAL AMOUNT BIANCA HAS SAVED IS REPRESENTED BY THE GRAPH OF A LINE THAT PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (0, 2) AND (2, 8). ">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_08_02.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00032">Which is greater, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>? Explain what this answer means.</para>
      <para id="para-00033"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, so after 2 days, Adam has saved more money.</para>
      <note class="try" id="note-00002">
  <title>Try It: Comparing Real-Life Functions</title>
      <para id="para-00034">Aleph is running at a constant rate on a flat, paved road. The graph below, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, represents the total distance, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, he covers with respect to time, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00035">
          <media alt="GRAPH THAT SHOWS TOTAL DISTANCE IN MILES AS A FUNCTION OF TIME IN MINUTES. THE GRAPH IS A STRAIGHT LINE THAT INCREASES FROM LEFT TO RIGHT AND PASSES THROUGH THE POINT (40, 5.5). ">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_08_03.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00036">Shannon is running on a flat, rocky trail that eventually rises up a steep mountain. The graph below, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>S</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, represents the total distance, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>S</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, she covers with respect to time, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00037">
          <media alt="GRAPH THAT SHOWS TOTAL DISTANCE IN MILES AS A FUNCTION OF TIME IN MINUTES. THE GRAPH IS NONLINEAR AND INCREASES FROM LEFT TO RIGHT AND INCLUDES THE POINT (40, 2.5).">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_08_04.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00003">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00038">Who has traveled farther after 40 minutes? Explain your answer.</para>
            <para id="para-00039">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
  </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00040">Here is how to determine who went a greater distance:</para>
            <para id="para-00041">Aleph traveled farther in 40 minutes. Comparing the graphs, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>40</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is 5.5 miles, and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>S</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>40</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is approximately 2.5 miles.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </note>
    </section>
        </section>
        
  </content>
